---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CtaSection from '../components/CtaSection.astro';
const site = (Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://algeriacompass.com').replace(/\/$/, '');
const aboutSchema = {
  '@type': 'AboutPage', '@id': `${site}/about/#about`,
  name: 'About Algeria Compass', url: `${site}/about/`,
  about: { '@id': `${site}/#organization` }, isPartOf: { '@id': `${site}/#website` },
};
const breadcrumb = { '@type':'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement:[
  {'@type':'ListItem',position:1,name:'Home',item:`${site}/`},
  {'@type':'ListItem',position:2,name:'About',item:`${site}/about/`}]};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Algeria Compass"
  description="Algeria Compass is a licensed Algerian tour operator with 7+ years guiding international travellers on private tours and Sahara expeditions across Algeria — rated 5.0 on Google. How we design itineraries and the standards we hold."
  image="/assets/img/brand-algeria.jpg"
  keywords={["about Algeria Compass","Algeria tour operator","licensed Algeria travel agency","private Algeria tours"]}
  schema={[aboutSchema, breadcrumb]}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{name:'Home',href:'/'},{name:'About'}]} />
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap" style="max-width:760px">
    <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
    <h1>Luxury private guided tours across Algeria</h1>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <p>Algeria Compass is a licensed Algerian tour operator dedicated entirely to one country. We design and operate private, guided journeys across Algeria — the largest country in Africa — with licensed local guides, and back every trip with deep, first-hand knowledge of the places we take you.</p>
      <p>We are not a brochure and not a listings site. We map Algeria as a connected whole: all 58 states, the seven UNESCO World Heritage Sites, the Roman cities of the north, the oasis worlds of the M'Zab and the Souf, the Kabyle mountains and the Mediterranean coast — and the food, history, languages and traditions that tie them together, explored in depth in our <a href="/discover/">guide to Algeria</a>.</p>

      <h2>Seven years guiding Algeria</h2>
      <p>Algeria Compass has worked in Algerian tourism for more than seven years, designing and leading private journeys for international travellers — from first-timers discovering the country to seasoned explorers returning for the deep south. In that time we have guided guests through the Ottoman Casbah of Algiers, the Roman cities of Tipaza, Djémila and Timgad, the Andalusian west and the Kabyle coast, and deep into the Sahara on multi-day desert expeditions around Djanet, Timimoun and the M'Zab Valley.</p>
      <p>Our two strengths sit side by side: running well-organised, genuinely private trips on the ground with licensed local guides, and pairing them with real cultural experiences — artisans, food, music and the everyday hospitality Algeria is known for. Travellers who have journeyed with us rate the experience <strong>5.0 out of 5 on Google</strong>, and the rating on our homepage links straight to those reviews so you can read them yourself.</p>

      <h2>Why we exist</h2>
      <p>Reliable, in-depth English-language information about Algeria is scarce and often out of date. Algeria Compass was created to fix that: to build, page by page, a trustworthy reference that treats the country with the seriousness it deserves and helps visitors travel with understanding and respect.</p>

      <h2>How we research</h2>
      <p>Every guide begins with research against primary and authoritative sources — UNESCO, recognised reference works, and established cultural and historical scholarship — set out in our <a href="/editorial/research-methodology/">research methodology</a>. Where a claim matters, we cite where it comes from; our approach to sourcing is described in our <a href="/editorial/sources-policy/">sources policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>How content is reviewed</h2>
      <p>Drafts are checked for accuracy before publication and pass through an independent <a href="/editorial/content-review-process/">review process</a>, separate from the writing, handled by our <a href="/reviewers/">review function</a>. Our wider standards are published in full in the <a href="/editorial/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>How we update and correct</h2>
      <p>Travel information ages. We revisit and refresh guides under a defined <a href="/editorial/content-update-policy/">update policy</a>, and when we get something wrong we fix it openly: anyone can flag an error through our <a href="/editorial/corrections-policy/">corrections policy</a>. We are transparent about how the platform works, including our limited and disclosed use of AI tooling — see our <a href="/editorial/transparency-policy/">transparency</a> and <a href="/editorial/ai-usage-policy/">AI-usage</a> policies.</p>

      <h2>Knowledge standards</h2>
      <p>Beneath the guides sits a structured <a href="/knowledge/">knowledge graph</a> of Algeria — states, heritage sites, landscapes, food and culture, modelled as connected entities so the relationships between places and themes are explicit and machine-readable. It is the backbone that keeps the platform consistent as it grows.</p>

      <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
      <p>Algeria Compass is produced by a team of Algerian travel and editorial specialists, working to the standards above. As we add named contributors and subject reviewers, they will appear on our <a href="/team/">editorial team</a> and <a href="/reviewers/">reviewers</a> pages, each shown against the work they are responsible for. We do not publish anonymous claims of expertise we cannot stand behind.</p>

      <h2>Mission and long-term vision</h2>
      <p>Our mission is simple: to become the most trusted, in-depth and respectful guide to Algeria in any language — the first place people turn to understand the country, and a reference that does justice to its history, landscapes and people. Over time we are building toward complete, sourced coverage of all 58 states and the major sites within them.</p>

      <p style="color:var(--text-l);font-size:.9rem">Algeria Compass designs and operates your private, guided journey end to end, with licensed local guides throughout. <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a> to plan your trip.</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <CtaSection />
</BaseLayout>
